* -y with -b on a 68020 (Ultra C's r68): every branch to a label 32-bit, an explicit .s too, and
* every PC-relative reference to a label the 32-bit (bd,PC) form, indexed too; a branch or a
* reference to a constant and dbcc as without. Without the option -y was refused.
* fixed: a9ea4bb 2026-10-13 r68togas: %-registers, -r, -y, the separate-files mode (-s, -x); docs brought up to date
* options: -y -b -m2
* expect text: 4e714e71 60fffffffffc 61ff00000000 6200000e 51c8ffec 41fb0170ffffffe8 43fb017000000000 323b0130ffffffd8 45fa0006
* expect reloc: R_68K_PC32        Ext
* expect reloc: R_68K_PC32        Ext+0x00000002
Disp equ 14
 psect long_refs,0,0,0,0,0
 nop
lab nop
 bra.s lab
 bsr Ext
 bhi Disp
 dbra d0,lab
 lea lab(pc),a0
 lea Ext(pc),a1
 move.w lab(pc,d0.w),d1
 lea 6(pc),a2
 ends
